import ../../../testing/driver.dl
import ../../../ui/floating_controls.dl
import ../../../ui/scene_labels.dl

appearance stage appearance:
    height is 300

document controls page:
    button "Before"
    button "After"
    view group "Stage views" using no UI appearance:
        region "Stage content" using no UI appearance:
            surface "Stage" using stage appearance
        region "Without stage" using no UI appearance:

appearance marker appearance:
    background is UI ink 30 50 40
    text is UI ink 240 235 210
    padding is 6
    font size is 12
    corner radius is 8

marker prototype means: (button "Person") wearing marker appearance

to [count floating click] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set count to instance's event context as a pointer to an integer
    set the value at count to (the value at count) + 1

to [click floating point] {UI point:point} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (point's x) (point's y) with modifiers 0 containing "" in view
    queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at (point's x) (point's y) with modifiers 0 containing "" in view
    queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at (point's x) (point's y) with modifiers 0 containing "" in view
    ignore update UI view view

to [remove floating click] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    remove UI floating control (instance's event context as a pointer to UI floating control)

to [paint empty stage] {a pointer to UI canvas frame:painting}:
    ignore painting

set clicks to 0
set instance to an instance of controls page
bind (the control labeled "Stage" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "paint empty stage $") for event 1
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 800 by 500 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
set controls to UI floating controls attached to (the control labeled "Stage" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of view)
set first to a UI floating control from marker prototype named (the string form of "alpha") in controls
set second to a UI floating control from marker prototype named (the string form of "beta") in controls
set {first node} to the address of (first's node)
set {second node} to the address of (second's node)
set UI text of (the address of (first's node)) in (the address of instance) to "Alex"
set UI text of (the address of (second's node)) in (the address of instance) to "Alex"
bind (the address of (first's node)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "count floating click $") for event 0 with context ((the address of clicks) as a pointer)
bind (the address of (second's node)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "count floating click $") for event 0 with context ((the address of clicks) as a pointer)
set viewport to UI box at 20 200 sized 700 260
place UI floating control first at (a UI point at 220.0 and 280.0) within viewport
place UI floating control second at (a UI point at 420.0 and 280.0) within viewport
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the address of (first's node)) != (the address of (second's node))) reporting "Repeated controls shared an identity"
set point to a UI point at (first's layout's painted bounds' x + 10.0) and (first's layout's painted bounds' y + 10.0)
require condition ((the UI hit at point in (the address of view)) = first's layout) reporting "The retained overlay did not expose the drawn button to hit testing"
set before to the UI layout labeled "Before" in (view's layout)
set point to a UI point at (before's painted bounds' x + 10.0) and (before's painted bounds' y + 10.0)
require condition ((the UI hit at point in (the address of view)) = before) reporting "A floating container intercepted the underlying page"
refresh UI focus in (the address of view)
require condition (view's control count = 4) reporting "Floating controls were omitted from keyboard navigation"
set the value of "Stage views" in (the address of instance) to -1
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
refresh UI focus in (the address of view)
require condition (((first's layout's paint generation = 0) and (second's layout's paint generation = 0)) and (view's control count = 2)) reporting "A hidden source surface retained floating controls"
set the value of "Stage views" in (the address of instance) to 0
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
refresh UI focus in (the address of view)
set view's focus order to 2
set view's keyboard focus to true
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 257 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition ((view's focused = first's layout) and (clicks = 1)) reporting "Tab and Enter did not activate the floating button through shared input"
set point to a UI point at (first's layout's painted bounds' x + 10.0) and (first's layout's painted bounds' y + 10.0)
click floating point point in (the address of view)
require condition ((view's hot = first's layout) and (clicks = 2)) reporting "The floating button did not use shared pointer activation"
set UI control first node enabled false in (the address of instance)
click floating point point in (the address of view)
require condition (clicks = 2) reporting "A disabled floating button remained interactive"
set UI control first node enabled true in (the address of instance)
hide UI floating control first
refresh UI focus in (the address of view)
require condition ((view's control count = 3) and (view's focused != first's layout)) reporting "A hidden floating button retained keyboard focus"
set camera to a UI scene camera at (a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 5.0) aimed at (a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0) with angle 45.0 aspect 1.0 near 0.1 far 100.0
project UI floating control first above (a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0) through camera in viewport
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (first's visible and (first's layout's hit bounds' width > 0.0)) reporting "A projected scene label did not become interactive"
project UI floating control first above (a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 6.0) through camera in viewport
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((first's visible = false) and (first's layout's paint generation = 0)) reporting "A label behind the camera remained visible"
remove UI floating control second
require condition ((controls's first = first) and (first's next = (0 as a pointer to UI floating control))) reporting "Removing a floating control left a list entry"
set removed to a UI floating control from marker prototype named (the string form of "self") in controls
bind (the address of (removed's node)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "remove floating click $") for event 0 with context (removed as a pointer)
place UI floating control removed at (a UI point at 500.0 and 320.0) within viewport
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set point to a UI point at (removed's layout's painted bounds' x + 10.0) and (removed's layout's painted bounds' y + 10.0)
click floating point point in (the address of view)
require condition (first's next = (0 as a pointer to UI floating control)) reporting "A floating button could not remove itself during activation"
close UI floating controls controls
require condition (view's overlays = (0 as a pointer to UI overlay)) reporting "Closing the control owner retained its overlay"
set entry to instance's values
loop while entry != (0 as a pointer to UI value):
    require condition ((entry's target != first node) and (entry's target != second node)) reporting "Removing controls retained their instance state"
    set entry to entry's next
require condition ((instance's handlers' target's text = "Stage") and (instance's handlers' next = (0 as a pointer to UI handler))) reporting "Removing controls retained their callbacks"
set controls to UI floating controls in (the address of view)
set automatic to a UI floating control from marker prototype named (the string form of "automatic") in controls
place UI floating control automatic at (a UI point at 300.0 and 300.0) within viewport
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
close the address of view
require condition (view's overlays = (0 as a pointer to UI overlay)) reporting "Closing a view did not release its floating controls"
close the address of instance
print line "Floating controls share painting, clipping, hit testing, keyboard activation, scene projection and owned lifetime."
